2026-09-21 | Stage 2 signed-media-URL helpers | The media endpoints need a credential a browser can actually present, without relaxing the rule that the API TOKEN never travels in a URL | Added sign_media / media_url / media_signature_is_valid / media_expiry to web/api/auth.py, in the stdlib-only region so they stay importable in the pytest-only CI env. Three choices worth naming: the signature covers the DECODED (job_id, filename, exp) triple rather than request.url.path, because a minted URL must percent-encode the filename and the path does not -- signing the path would 401 on exactly the names containing a space or non-ASCII char and on no others; the payload is length-prefixed so ("a|b","c") and ("a","b|c") cannot collide; and the key is HMAC(token, context) rather than the token itself, so a captured signature gives nothing to grind against the real credential. exp is QUANTISED into buckets of ttl/2 -- without that, every response mints a different URL for the same file, and changing a <video> src tears down playback and discards the cached bytes | web/api/auth.py, tests/test_media_urls.py (37 tests)
